%N A071443 Sprague-Grundy values for octal game .113337.
%C A071443 Octal game .01337 has values a(n-1). Octal game .0037 has values a(n-2). Octal game .006 has values a(n-3).
%C A071443 a(n) is also the Sprague-Grundy value of a heap of n+3 tokens in the octal game .006; equivalently, the Sprague-Grundy sequence of .006 is 0, 0, 0, 0, followed by this sequence. - _Tyler Satchel Orden_, Aug 05 2026
%C A071443 Computed (as the game .006) through heap size 2^27 = 134217728 by Tyler Satchel Orden (2026), extending A. Flammenkamp's tables for .006, which reached 2^26. All of Flammenkamp's published invariants at 2^26 (487832 rare values in his sparse-space sense, last at heap size 67104903; maximum value 6580, first at heap size 26683203) were reproduced exactly before extending. Beyond 2^26 the sparse set remains active: 2932 further rare values appear, the last at heap size 134149764, with values in the interval [1537, 4605]; the maximum value is unchanged. - _Tyler Satchel Orden_, Aug 05 2026
